  buildingName: Storefront
  buildingRole: 3
  description: '"The sign still says groceries. That is the point."


    A small
    storefront gives the operation a face. People come and go without raising immediate
    suspicion, and product can move through the district faster. But every extra
    customer is another pattern someone can notice.'
  hasProductionControls: 1
  requiresPurchase: 0
  isPurchased: 1
  purchaseCost: 450
  purchaseButtonText: "Buy the storefront (-450 \u20AC)"
  purchaseDescription: Before you can use this place, you need to buy the lease,
    stock the shelves, and make the front believable. It is expensive, but it opens
    a steady way to move product.
  showIncreaseAction: 0
  showDecreaseAction: 0
  actionsChangeLevel: 1
  actionCooldownEvents: 1
  productionLevel: 0
  minProductionLevel: -2
  maxProductionLevel: 2
  productionDescription: You choose how loudly the storefront works. Pushing sales
    brings money and reputation, but also heat. Keeping it quiet slows income and
    lowers risk. After each move, one event must pass before the storefront can be
    adjusted again.
  statusName: Distribution pressure
  neutralStatusText: controlled
  positiveStatusText: aggressive
  negativeStatusText: quiet
  increaseButtonText: Push distribution
  decreaseButtonText: Keep it quiet
  increaseNovac: 80
  increaseRizik: 8
